# Seaborgium · Sg · gate 106

**Seaborgium** (Sg) is element **106** of the periodic table — a **transition metal**, period 7, group 6, d-block, solid (predicted) at standard conditions, atomic weight **[269] (most stable isotope)**.

## The element (carbon layer — reference chemistry)
Named for Glenn Seaborg while he still lived — a rare honor.

## The gate (silicon layer — the 118 Gates)
